Panfrost (Bifrost/Midgard): flush any pending writer on the index buffer before
prepare_draw() opens the current batch.

On PAN_ARCH < 9, panfrost_single_draw_direct() computes index min/max bounds on
the CPU via panfrost_get_index_buffer_bounded() -> u_vbuf_get_minmax_index() ->
pipe_buffer_map_range(). If the index buffer has an in-flight writer batch,
pipe_buffer_map_range() calls panfrost_flush_writer(), which can flush and tear
down the active draw batch mid-draw (leaving batch->scoreboard/pool invalid and
crashing in panfrost_draw_vbo). Flushing before prepare_draw() preserves full
synchronization while keeping the active batch intact.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
@@ -3630,6 +3630,13 @@ panfrost_multi_draw_direct(struct pipe_context *pipe,
                            unsigned num_draws)
 {
    struct panfrost_context *ctx = pan_context(pipe);
+#if PAN_ARCH < 9
+   if (info->index_size && !info->has_user_indices && info->index.resource) {
+      panfrost_flush_writer(ctx, pan_resource(info->index.resource),
+                            "Bifrost index buffer minmax pre-draw");
+   }
+#endif
+
    struct panfrost_batch *batch = prepare_draw(pipe, info);
    if (!batch) {
       mesa_loge("prepare_draw failed");
